{"id": "EUVD-2026-55586", "enisaUuid": "ca8dcee9-6aec-3627-9f5b-6539a82460b9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfirmware: arm_ffa: Fix Endpoint Memory Access Descriptor offset calculation\n\nUse the descriptor's `ep_mem_offset` to calculate the start of the endpoint\nmemory access array and to comply with the FF-A spec instead of defaulting\nto `sizeof(struct ffa_mem_region)`.\nThis requires moving `ffa_mem_region_additional_setup()` earlier in the setup\nflow.\nAlso, add sanity checks to ensure the calculated descriptor offsets do not\nexceed `max_fragsize`.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:04:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:43:58", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e902bea625b710f8bf2f40b4ae4b14fa6a33f13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b39b08e6bee812514b449dc874076890e6b871a0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ef18f0ab3c0ec1eac77289f5a542bd96a8a6d66", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b4d961351aa84fdf0148783fb1f3a1391b8a0adb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-68400", "GHSA-9fc3-h9fc-q4xw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f5f0ebf-32df-3e1a-b090-97b319708fc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "2723256a-56ba-3d7b-8f7e-d428061f6b89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "113580530ee7dc61e668b641d657920734533b9f <b39b08e6bee812514b449dc874076890e6b871a0"}, {"id": "7258a510-45cb-379a-99db-fbf07098a499", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "113580530ee7dc61e668b641d657920734533b9f <b4d961351aa84fdf0148783fb1f3a1391b8a0adb"}, {"id": "757d8523-5bc5-3eaa-8248-e279623c2a22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "76bcb068-d2bb-3b5f-8bed-de814e05c3bc", "product": {